\ A parameter{ } default quotation runs under the interpreter on an unbound
\ get. The freeze BFS must walk that default and seed the words it calls into
\ the compilation set. Otherwise a callee reachable only through the default
\ has its interpretable body dropped as empty with no compiled function, so
\ calling it is a silent no-op that leaks the caller's inputs.
\
\ Here `seconds` is reached only through the default. Without the discovery
\ fix `idle-timeout get` drops `seconds` and yields the bare fixnum 30 instead
\ of a duration.

use "time" ;

idle-timeout: parameter{ [ 30 seconds ] } ;

idle-timeout get duration? >string print-line      \ t once seconds runs
idle-timeout get duration-nsec >string print-line  \ 30000000000
